@page
@model IndexModel
@{
	ViewData["Title"] = "Home page";
}

<div class="text-left">
	<h1 class="display-4">Welcome</h1>
	<p>
		This sample application demonstrates the use of DevExtreme controls by tag helpers.
		Tag helpers are a mechanism used by Microsoft ASP.Net Core to enable server-side code to participate in creating and rendering HTML elements in Razor files.
		DevExpress has started an open source project to create tag helpers for their controls, but seemingly abandoned that effort.
		We like the use of tag helpers, and have have therefore created this project.
	</p>
	<p>
		This sample application does not reference any Alcazar Nuget packages, other than what is required for <strong>Alcazar.DevExpress.TagHelpers</strong>,
		and does therefore not depend on and implement the Alcazar ASP.Net One framework.
	</p>
	<p>
		<a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/mvc/views/tag-helpers/intro">See what Microsoft says</a>
	</p>
</div>
